{
  "raw": {
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Facilities-Management/Athletic-Field-Specialist_JR100599": {
      "title": "Athletic Field Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Facilities Management - Grounds and Landscaping Position Details This position serves as the specialist responsible for the care, growth, appearance, maintenance and safety of athletic fields and athletic complex grounds. Additionally, the Athletic Field Specialist functions as a working member of College’s grounds crew (Groundskeeper I), in performing various duties to maintain and assure the attractive appearance of campus through daily execution of planned maintenance activities. Crew members are expected to maintain their individual campus zone with minimal supervision and direction. Crew members should be able to plan, prioritize and execute their activities such that the required work gets done with minimal intervention from their supervisor(s). Essential Functions Maintains natural and synthetic athletic fields and grounds to a professional level. This includes fertilization, aerification, pest and disease monitoring and treatment, turf grass establishment and overseeding, turf grass and landscape weed control, ancillary field maintenance including management of infield and warning track surfaces. Completes grooming, mowing, trimming and other turf grass maintenance activities in secondary areas of Dickinson Park and Biddle Field. Ensures work is done in a safe, professional, and productive manor. Attends seminars and safety training as required by the Director of Grounds. Maintains pesticide applicator certification via update trainings. Maintains pesticide application log. Operate, maintain and monitor automatic irrigation systems and repair as needed. Maintain and repair equipment to include mowers, sprayers, tractors, field rakes, etc. Blade sharpening. Weekly safety monitoring of all equipment. Assist with snow removal from campus sidewalks, parking lots, driveways and steps. All grounds crew members are considered “emergency response personnel.” As such they are required to report to work even when the college is closed or is operating under a delayed start. Grounds crew members can be called in at any time of day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. It is expected that the employee has reliable transportation adequate to transport them to work even under adverse weather conditions. Requirements Associate's Degree - Horticulture, turf grass management, agronomy. This position requires a  valid driver's license for the operation of a company owned, rented or leased vehicle Preferred: Bachelor's degree - Horticulture, turf grass management, agronomy. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Utility-Worker-Dining-Hall_JR100597": {
      "title": "Utility Worker Dining Hall",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Kitchen Position Details The position is responsible for cleanliness and aesthetics of all dining services areas in the front-of-house and back-of house. Duties include waste and recycling removal; sweeping, scrubbing, and mopping floors; assisting culinary team and retail operations staff with cleaning of equipment; pot and pan/utensil ware washing operations; restroom maintenance; shampooing carpet and waxing/sealing floors; cleaning of receiving dock areas to include washing dumpsters and sweeping parking lot areas. Essential Functions: Cleaning and sanitizing all kitchen and catering supplies and returning them to their proper location according to the guidelines established by the department. Maintains all floors, walls and equipment throughout the department in a clean, safe and sanitary manner. Cleans and sanitizes employee restrooms on a daily basis. Maintains all paper towel dispensers and cleaning supplies and reports all supply needs to the Dining Hall Manager. Cleans all kitchen equipment according to the guidelines established by the department. Maintains a clean, safe and sanitary work environment throughout the shift. Performs any other related duties as assigned by management.    This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience and knowledge of cleaning and sanitation is preferred. The ability to work independently and stay focused on daily job responsibilities is essential. The ability to interact and communicate with co- workers is necessary. Serv-Safe Certification is preferred or must be obtained within one year of hire date. Physical Demands: Must have the ability to lift 30 pounds on a regular basis and occasionally 50 pounds. The position requires the employee to constantly stand, bend, reach, twist, stoop and walk. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Old-West-College/Access-and-Operations-Coordinator_JR100594": {
      "title": "Access and Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department ADS and SOAR Position Details Join an energetic, collaborative, and student-centered team, dedicated to providing strategic guidance and facilitating equitable access for hundreds of Dickinson students with disabilities. This position offers a wealth of opportunities for a resourceful professional with excellent communication skills who enjoys problem-solving, thoughtful decision-making, organizing multifaceted processes, making an impact, and working closely with college students and their professors. The chosen candidate can expect ample training, professional development, and team support, along with the gratification that comes with witnessing the meaningful difference made by the work that we do. Position Summary The Access and Operations Coordinator plays an integral role in ensuring that the strategy resources and accommodation services relied upon by Dickinson students, faculty, and campus partners are administered effectively, accurately, and in accordance with disability law. The Coordinator guides individuals through accommodation processes; organizes, tracks, reviews, and summarizes confidential disclosure information and documentation; collaborates to administer thousands of proctored exams; optimizes the timely determination and implementation of disability accommodations; and manages an array of logistical, administrative, communication, and operational responsibilities for the busy offices of Access and Disability Services (ADS) and Strategies, Organization, & Achievement Resources (SOAR). Essential Functions Access and Resource Guidance: Guide current and prospective students, parents, care providers, faculty, and campus partners through the ADS accommodation processes for students with disabilities (which may be neurological, developmental, emotional/behavioral, or physical), as well as those seeking study and time management support through SOAR. Communicate with accuracy, patience, discretion, and respect. Assess the nature and urgency of each inquiry, which may be sensitive or complex, and determine how best to resolve matters and/or connect individuals with the appropriate individual or resource. Proctoring and Accommodation Implementation: Co-facilitate the administration of timed assessments for students with test-taking accommodations. Review granted accommodations and the requirements of each exam to determine appropriate arrangements necessary for space, staffing, assistive technology, materials, and other resources. Communicate with students and faculty to clarify expectations, address incomplete or conflicting information, and respond to changes in scheduling or testing needs. Help maintain the security and academic integrity of the testing environment and ensure that completed exams are securely delivered. Oversee all “end-of-the-day” exam proctoring and the Proctoring Center, including test-takers, student proctors, and any temporary staff, and independently resolve any issues that may arise. Confidential Records, Workflow, and Process Administration: Co-manage confidential accommodation records, complex databases, and case workflows for approximately 500 students, including requests, functional-impact information, documentation, communications, meeting notes, determinations, implementation steps, and follow-up. Monitor unresolved items, establish priorities, and take appropriate steps to address actions needed. Produce useful and accurate reports and use data and operational knowledge to recommend and implement improvements to forms, communications, information systems, and procedures to improve usability, efficiency, and accessibility. Accommodation Review and Determination : Conduct individualized reviews of assigned accommodation requests that may be related to academic, housing, dietary, or mobility needs. Apply training given to analyze disability documentation, recommendations for accommodation, and the student’s description of functional limitations and access barriers. Weigh potential options, and exercise independent judgment to determine and document reasonable accommodations. Department Operations and Resource Management: Manage responsibilities that ensure the smooth operation of the ADS & SOAR department, including inventory, purchasing, expense reconciliation, form creation, webpage revisions, and the organization of the main office. Evaluate needs and available resources, recommend or make expenditures, maintain accurate records, and advise about future requirements, workflow concerns, and opportunities to improve departmental effectiveness. Assist with training, scheduling, and reviewing the work of student employees and casual staff, as assigned. Continuity of Access Services: Develop working knowledge of the essential accommodation services across the department to ensure coverage when colleagues are unavailable. Apply learned protocols and sound judgment to sustain timely services such as the loan of assistive technology, the facilitation of supplemental notes, access to texts in an accessible format, and real-time captioning. Collaborate to support team members’ time off so that all granted accommodations are implemented seamlessly. Other Duties and Responsibilities Because the work frequently involves competing priorities, individualized circumstances, sensitive information, and questions for which the appropriate response is not always immediately evident, the Coordinator must exercise discretion, sound judgment, and appropriate independence while recognizing when input from others is needed. Plan and organize assigned work, establish priorities, and adjust workflows in response to changing student and departmental needs. Participate in departmental planning and contribute informed recommendations concerning policies, practices, communications, and service delivery. Handle confidential disability and student information with discretion and in accordance with applicable law and college policy. Develop and maintain current knowledge of relevant college policies and protocols, disability case law and best practices, and departmental systems and practices. Other Duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Guides work of others who perform essentially the same work. May organize, set priorities, schedule, and review work, but has no responsibility to hire, terminate, review performance, or make pay decisions. Requirements Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, relevant training, and relevant professional administrative experience. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to respond constructively to unanticipated or sensitive questions or concerns. Strong organizational, time management, and project coordination skills, with the ability to prioritize competing responsibilities and meet time-sensitive deadlines. Demonstrated analytical and real-time problem-solving abilities. Experience reviewing complex information, applying policies or standards, and making consequential decisions. Strong computer skills and proficiency with Microsoft Office 365 applications, including calendar scheduling, Word documents, mail merges, and advanced knowledge of Excel formulas and functions, and an ability to learn new systems and technologies. Ability to follow instructions well, to work both independently and collaboratively, to seek consultation when appropriate, and to contribute to a supportive, solution-focused team environment. Commitment to providing responsive, inclusive, and respectful service for individuals with varied identities, experiences, communication styles, and access needs. Ability to oversee the proctoring of exams until 6 pm, as needed. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a higher education setting. Experience working directly with young adults. Experience with disability accommodations, accessibility, student support, compliance, and/or individualized case review. Knowledge about and/or relevant experience with individuals with disabilities. Experience using a database or a case-management system. Minimum Work Experience 3-5 years of relevant work experience Independence of Action Results are defined; incumbent sets own goals and determines how to accomplish results with few or no guidelines to follow, although precedents may exist; supervisor/manager provides broad guidance and overall direction. Equipment Used Computer Telephone Printer/scanner/copier Departmental databases Microsoft 365 applications Physical and Environmental Demands Office environment No specific physical demands EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/42-Cherry-St/Wellness-Outreach-Coordinator-Counselor_JR100592": {
      "title": "Wellness Outreach Coordinator/Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nPart time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Wellness Center - CAPS Position Details Position Department Wellness Center Position Details Position Summary The Outreach Coordinator/Counselor supports the Wellness Center's mission by facilitating psychoeducational workshops and campus wellness outreach programs. Oversees the Peer Educator Program, guiding student leaders in promoting health and wellness. Provides mental health services to students, including initial consultations and intakes and individual or group therapy. Essential Functions Oversee peer educator program, design and deliver training programs to ensure peer educators are prepared to effectively support program goals, provide accurate information, and model appropriate professional and ethical standards. Coordinate peer educator work schedules, including timesheet approval, and assignments to ensure effective delivery of grant-compliant outreach activities. Provide ongoing coaching, mentorship, and feedback, fostering a positive experience/environment. Lead the planning, coordination, implementation, and assessment of wellness outreach programming. Collaborate with colleagues to develop and deliver departmental programs that support student well-being and institutional priorities. Develop and deliver student-focused psychoeducation workshops covering the dimensions of wellness. Maintain accurate documentation of programs, attendance, and participant feedback. Provide clinical counseling and psychological services including but not limited to initial consultations, intakes, individual and group therapy, crisis intervention, and ongoing consultations. Other Duties and Responsibilities Other duties may include providing case management services and participating in center outreach or educational activities. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Master's degree in Social Work, Counseling, Clinical Psychology or related field, required. Licensed as a mental health professional in Pennsylvania, required. Minimum Work Experience 1 to 3 years of relevant experience. Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Standard office equipment including desktop computer, phone, copier/printer/fax machine. Physical/Environmental Demands Office environment. Specific physical requirements or environmental exposures. Infectious Diseases: Employees are frequently exposed to contagious or infectious diseases. Exposure to Animals: Working in laboratories with animals. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/50-Mooreland-Ave/Photographer---Digital-Creator_JR100584": {
      "title": "Photographer and Digital Creator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Marketing & Communication - Visual Media Position Details This is a creative position for someone with great visual instincts, stays ahead of visual and social trends, and brings a fresh and energetic perspective to the way Dickinson tells its story. Position Summary Creates vibrant, compelling visual content for the Office of Marketing and Communications, with photography serving as a central focus of the role. Captures events, portraits, campus life, branding imagery and social media content with a creative eye and strong understanding of visual storytelling. Brings awareness of current digital trends and audience engagement strategies to develop fresh, authentic content that reflects the Dickinson experience and supports the college’s communications goals. Assists with higher-level video productions, including filming, lighting, audio and other on-location production needs. Occasional evening and weekend work is required to support campus events and related assignments. Essential Functions Bring the Dickinson story to life through fresh, creative photography for the website, social media, print and digital marketing. Create dynamic, audience-focused social media content that sparks interest, encourages sharing, and strengthens brand visibility by transforming ideas into engaging digital experiences. Plan and deliver compelling photographic coverage of campus events and activities, including select evening and weekend assignments, to create, engaging visual content that enhances storytelling, builds community connections, and promotes institutional pride. Lend creative and technical experience int he development and production of high-quality video productions. Mentor and collaborate with student workers and social media ambassadors to brainstorm, test, and create content that feels authentic to the Dickinson student experience while building community. Other Duties and Responsibilities Involvement in developing messaging particularly as it involves visual content. Gear maintenance. Working with student photography positions. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Bachelor's degree required in Photography, Digital Media, Marketing, Communications or related field. Portfolio that demonstrates previous professional photography and video production experience Portfolio should highlight ability to photograph both events and portraits, as well as professional video production. Experience with the Adobe Creative Cloud including, but not limited to Premiere, Photoshop and Lightroom. Ability to work a flexible schedule including occasional evenings and weekends. Ability for some travel. Minimum Work Experience 3-5 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Sony Alpha-series mirrorless cameras. SLR lenses Lights Tripod Adobe editing software General office equipment Physical/Environmental Demands Specific physical requirements or environmental exposures Outdoor Environment: Employee work outdoors and may not be protected from weather conditions. Hazards: Includes a variety of physical conditions, such as proximity to moving mechanical parts, moving vehicles, electrical current, working on scaffolding and high places, or exposure to chemicals. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/South-College-WEST-Fin-Aid/Temporary-Financial-Aid-Specialist_JR100589": {
      "title": "Temporary Financial Aid Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Financial Aid Position Details This is a temporary, full-time position for a one-year term, with a possibility of extension. Summary The Financial Aid Specialist will be responsible for reviewing institutional and federal financial aid applications, determining financial aid eligibility, and creating financial aid offers, using Dickinson’s financial aid system, PowerFAIDS. This person will be responsible for Senior Associate and Director level work. Serves as a professional resource for staff/system given knowledge and expertise in PowerFAIDS. May conduct Q/A sessions as learn new system. Based on past experience, may contribute insights to practices and new system. This role also entails supporting the Loan Specialist with Federal Direct Loan and private/alternative loan certification. This individual will ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional financial aid policies. Essential Functions Review financial aid applications, resolve conflicting information, and package prospective and returning student financial aid to ensure affordability while meeting the college's enrollment, retention, and financial goals. Verify student eligibility for institutional, federal, and state financial aid by reconciliation of differences between the Free Application for Federal Student Aid and CSS profile and confirming eligibility after thorough verification of documents including parent and student tax return, W-2 forms and other required verification worksheets. Ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional policies, and participation in training opportunities and webinars to stay current on regulation changes. Review and process Federal Direct Loan and private/alternative loan application as needed. Other Duties and Responsibilities Resolve over awards. Meet virtually with students regarding financial aid questions. Assist in clean up reports. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Associate's degree, required. Bachelor's degree, preferred Prior experience with financial aid packaging in PowerFAIDS Demonstrated knowledge of financial aid application process Prior experience with College's Board CSS Profile and institutional methodology Ability to comply with all federal, state, and institutional policies Ability to work independently, take initiative, and follow through on tasks with minimal supervision Strong written and verbal communication skills, organization and time-management skills Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines, professional judgement, discretion, and a collaborative approach to working across departments, strong partnerships, with a service orientation and genuine interest in institutional mission Work Experience 3-5 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Standard office equipment Physical/Environmental Demands Office environment No specific or unusual physical demands EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Carlisle-Pennsylvania/Communications-Officer_JR100583": {
      "title": "Communications Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Public Safety Position Details Dispatcher To support campus law enforcement and other public safety functions by performing activities related to processing service requests and questions; which include communications and dispatch, status monitoring, information development and communication, and records and file maintenance in a computer-aided environment. The Communications Center serves as the primary link between the public and DPS Police Officers in the field. The Communications Center is the central coordinating agency for emergency telephone calls and requests for assistance. After hours the Communications Center serves as the main information, responsible for aiding the college community and its guests with requests for service and general inquiries. Essential Functions Handles emergency and non-emergency telephone calls, prioritizes calls, and channels pertinent information to officer and supervisory personnel. Makes necessary emergency notifications. Monitors and operates police and other radio systems, fire and intrusion alarm systems, and security camera systems, and dispatches officers and other emergency personnel as needed. Monitors computer terminals for messages directed to the Department, information related to local criminal activity, and officer safety messages. Confirms warrants with responsible agencies. Provides the public with assistance on complaints and informational services, lost and found property, bicycle registration, directions, and other services. Uses tact and discretion. Observes strict confidentiality rules. Directs persons to proper supervisory level as necessary. Accurately documents officer status, location and activity. Preserves accurate logs of incoming service requests and action taken and enters, updates, and recovers information from a Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) system. Preserves and updates various logs and records of activities, such as radio transmissions, telephone calls, tow requests, and equipment failure logs. Demonstrates knowledge of police terminology and procedures, Pennsylvania criminal and civil law as it pertains to police communications, campus geography, police services, and College policies and procedures pertaining to police communications. Provides assistance and information to persons registering vehicles at Public Safety and issues parking decals. Performs various tasks to ensure proper operation of equipment such as setting and resetting computer system, video display terminals, and printers. Assists with College fleet reservations and issues keys for reserved fleet vehicles. Required: High School Diploma or GED EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Kline-Life-Sports-Learning-Complex/Lifeguard_JR100557": {
      "title": "Lifeguard",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nVariable time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Athletics - Aquatics - Student Worker Administration Position Details This position performs lifeguard duties at the Kline Center Pool. Preferred Qualifications: Must be 16 years of age and have current certification in Lifeguarding, First Aid, and CPR.   Required documents: Uploaded certifications for Lifeguarding and CPR/First Aid.    Specific safety guidelines will be provided to employees, in accordance with state regulations. All individuals, including visitors, on campus are required to wear masks and follow appropriate CDC social distancing procedures at all times. Please note that employment as a Lifeguard is not able to be performed remotely. Employment and payment for hours worked will cease upon leaving campus.   Supervise all bathers/swimmers Enforce pool rules for bathers/swimmers Perform safety checks to ensure a safe facility Monitor pool water chemistry, air and water temperature Maintain current certification in Lifeguarding, First Aid and CPR Participate in in-service training for emergency procedures The pool cannot be open without appropriate and qualified staffing. This includes use by Athletic teams, Students, Faculty, Staff and Alumni Requires special skills, knowledge, or abilities. Work entails general guidelines. Moderate level of work experience or knowledge is required (minimum 6 months). Possess the knowledge and skills to perform independently with or without training. Person will have limited supervision. They will have some decision-making authority.   EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dining-Service---Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Casual-Caterer_JR100587": {
      "title": "Casual Caterer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nVariable time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department JM - Dining Services - Catering Position Details Dining Services supports campus food service operations. This role is ideal for individuals who enjoy working in a fast-paced environment and are committed to providing quality service to students, faculty, and staff. Job Description Assist with set up, execution, and clean-up of catered events. Essential Functions: Safe food handling practices Customer service Organizational Skills Follow Directions Serve food to event patrons Load/Unload catering trucks Work Required events/shifts as specified Bartender Specifics: Must be a minimum of 18 years old and hold a current RAMP or TIPS certification Verify identification and age requirements Prepare and responsibly serve alcoholic beverages including traditional mixed cocktails, wine bottle service and champagne service Bar set up/and tear-down/inventory and proper storage of beer, wine and liquor Marginal Functions: Occasionally work independently Proactively anticipate items needed for various functions Equipment Used: Carts, food warmers, ice machine, beverage dispensers etc. Other food service equipment, utensils, and dishes Must be 16 years old This position requires the employee to stand constantly and/or walk during the entire 4-5 hour shift, occasionally use stairs and work outdoors on an uneven surface. It also requires the employee to lift up to 50 pounds on a regular basis. Hours will vary including days, evenings and weekends. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Landis-House/Administrative-Assistant-Diversity--Equity--and-Inclusivity_JR100578": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant Diversity, Equity, and Inclusivity",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Women's and Gender Resource Center Position Details Position Summary Under the supervision of the Director of the Women’s Gender Resource Center, the Administrative Associate for Equity/Inclusivity will perform varied advanced secretarial and administrative work for the Office. This includes providing support for the Women’s and Gender Resource Center, the Popel Shaw Center for Race and Ethnicity, the Office of LGBTQ Services, and student workers. This position may have contact with high-level administrative offices and other campus departments and must be able to respond as appropriate. Essential Functions Interpret and explain established policies and procedures in response to inquiries from a variety of sources. Summarizing reports and information to facilitate review by supervisor, and investigating, evaluating and resolving problems within the scope of position. Maintains department files, record-keeping systems, and confidential materials. Provides office operations support such as receiving and screening telephone calls and visitors, scheduling meetings, conference, seminars, and special events, maintaining supervisor’s calendar. Utilizes, maintains and updates databases, software applications, and spreadsheets. Generate letters, forms, reports, mailings, requests, faxes, credit card statements, office procedures, etc. Prepares minutes, notices, manuals, agendas and correspondence with all supporting documentation, requiring application of specialized knowledge of the assigned function. Monitors and updates inventory, time, budget, payroll, and account records for office, monitors expenditures and performs simple analysis on accounts, authorizes and/or approves payments within established guidelines. Other Duties and Responsibilities Arranges necessary travel reservations and itineraries. Anticipates, and prepares background materials needed. Implements new policies, procedures, practices impacted by decisions made by directors at meetings and/or conferences. Coordinates student assistants including training, payroll, etc. departmental and student development staff. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervision Not responsible for supervising others. Education/Requirements High school diploma or GED, required. Bachelor's degree, preferred. Additional years of directly-related office experience may substitute some education. Valid driver's license, preferred. Experience 1 to 3 years of relevant experience. Independence of Action Work progress is monitored by supervisor/manager; incumbent follows precedents and procedures, and may set priorities and organizes work within general guidelines established by supervisor/manager. Work Environment Office environment/no specific or unusual physical or environmental demands. Equipment/Tools Used Standard office equipment including computer, copier/printer, etc. Microsoft Office Suite. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Carlisle-Pennsylvania/Communications-Officer_JR100563": {
      "title": "Communications Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Public Safety Position Details To support campus law enforcement and other public safety functions by performing activities related to processing service requests and questions; which include communications and dispatch, status monitoring, information development and communication, and records and file maintenance in a computer-aided environment. The Communications Center serves as the primary link between the public and DPS Police Officers in the field. The Communications Center is the central coordinating agency for emergency telephone calls and requests for assistance. After hours the Communications Center serves as the main information, responsible for aiding the college community and its guests with requests for service and general inquiries. Essential Functions Handles emergency and non-emergency telephone calls, prioritizes calls, and channels pertinent information to officer and supervisory personnel. Makes necessary emergency notifications. Monitors and operates police and other radio systems, fire and intrusion alarm systems, and security camera systems, and dispatches officers and other emergency personnel as needed. Monitors computer terminals for messages directed to the Department, information related to local criminal activity, and officer safety messages. Confirms warrants with responsible agencies. Provides the public with assistance on complaints and informational services, lost and found property, bicycle registration, directions, and other services. Uses tact and discretion. Observes strict confidentiality rules. Directs persons to proper supervisory level as necessary. Accurately documents officer status, location and activity. Preserves accurate logs of incoming service requests and action taken and enters, updates, and recovers information from a Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) system. Preserves and updates various logs and records of activities, such as radio transmissions, telephone calls, tow requests, and equipment failure logs. Demonstrates knowledge of police terminology and procedures, Pennsylvania criminal and civil law as it pertains to police communications, campus geography, police services, and College policies and procedures pertaining to police communications. Provides assistance and information to persons registering vehicles at Public Safety and issues parking decals. Performs various tasks to ensure proper operation of equipment such as setting and resetting computer system, video display terminals, and printers. Assists with College fleet reservations and issues keys for reserved fleet vehicles. Required: High School Diploma or GED EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/East-College/Assistant-Professor-of-Religion_JR100572": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Religion",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Academics - Religion Position Details The Robert H. N. Ho Family Foundation Professor in Buddhist Studies at Dickinson College       The Religion Department invites applications for a tenure-track position in Buddhis t Studies with demonstrated competence in the field of Religious Studies at the rank of assistant professor beginning in Fall 2027 . We are open to candidates whose work focuses in any era, and in any geographical region (including transnational and diasporic studies of Buddhism). The successfu l candidate w ill be able to contribute to campus and department needs in one or more of the following are a s: s ustainability and development , i nterreli gious encounters, negotiations, and/or dialogue . The teaching load is five courses per year in addition to advising senior theses.   The successful candidate will hold the title of The Robert H. N. Ho Family Foundation Professor of Buddhist Studies for the first four years in the position and must have a Ph.D. in religious studies or a related field in hand by the start of appointment and demonstrate an ability to teac h in Buddhis t Studies as well as core Religious Studies courses. Further desirable qualifications include competence in other languages relevant to the study of Buddhism ( e.g. Sanskri , Pali, classical Chinese, and/or vernacular Asian language) . The Department is seeking outstanding   candidates with the potential for exceptional teaching and research. Candidates must have the ability to create learning environments that are inclusive and welcoming to all students.   Learn more about the Department at: https://www.dickinson.edu/homepage/105/religion_department   The incoming colleague will teach courses in their area of expertise in addition to the department’s core courses on rotation , including Buddhism; Buddhism and the Environment; Contemplative Practices in Asia; and Religions of Asia. In addition, they will be given support to develop at least two new courses during their pre-tenure cycle; this will include courses that incorporate the faculty’s expertise alongside key themes of sustainability, deve lopment, and global exchange. The College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, religion, age, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or any other protected class. We encourage applications from all qualified persons.   This is a full-time, benefits-eligible position . Questions about this position should be directed to the chair of the search committee, Professor Peter Schadler schadler@dickinson.edu . Candidates should submit via Workday (online application system) at https://jobs.dickinson.edu ; please submit a cover letter , a CV , a teaching statement, a research statement, graduate transcript, names and contact information for three confidential recommenders (full recommendation letters will be sought at a later stage) . Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and continue until the posit ion is filled.   EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dickinson-College/Salad-Department-Worker_JR100569": {
      "title": "Salad Department Worker",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Kitchen Job Summary/Basic Function Salad Department workers are responsible for preparing all cold food items produced in the salad Department according to guidelines established by Dining Services, to include a variety of cooking methods and equipment. Workers are responsible for setting up appropriate sauce bars, condiment bars, pre-meal coffee brewing, and other special dining room stations for themed menus, events, and special salad bar menus. Workers are responsible for coordinating pick-up of catering orders and assembly of items for function sheets/catered events and retail locations, including the drawing of beverages, brewing coffee, and the preparation of retail crudités, yogurt parfaits, and fruit bowls/cups and salads. Essential Duties: Produces colorful eye appealing tasty daily dining hall breakfast bar, salad bar, and Grab & Go items following established par stock levels, standardized recipes. and defined procedures. Prepares specialty bar ingredients and topping or condiment bars for catered functions and dining hall events or themed meals according to the guidelines and standard recipes established by the Executive Chef or Sous Chef for Catering. Ensures safety of self, co-workers, and customers by maintaining a clean and neat, safe and sanitary work place following ServSafe procedures, HACCP guidelines, and OSHA regulations or college policies. Prepares food items for retail operations; includes parfait cups, crudité cups, to-go salads, and to-go fruit containers. Responsible for special function board items for any special production items or products necessary for catered events, assigned pick-up items, dining hall menus, events, themed meal programs, and draws beverages for “function sheet” orders; coordinates delivery of pick-up items, desserts, and salads for picnics, catered functions, etc. Assists in new product and recipe development. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed.   Other Duties May Include: Track amounts of product used at assigned station. Report amount to chef for record purposes. Monitor dates on product boxes to double check FIFO. Return copies of all cash operation orders, as they are filled to proper location for billing purposes. Required Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED with 1-3 years of relevant work experience. Preferred Qualifications: Vocational or technical certificate/degree in Culinary Arts. Serv-Safe certified or obtain certification within one year of hire. Physical Demands: This position requires the employee to stand the entire shift and lift 50 pounds on a regular basis. The position also requires bending, twisting and stooping. Work Schedule This position will work both day and evening shifts starting as early as 6:00 a.m. and working as late as 10:00 p.m. for a total of 40 hours. Days off will vary depending on business needs. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Cook_JR100567": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Kitchen Job Summary/Basic Function This is a hands-on food production position. The cook must have the ability to work in all production stations in the kitchen, dining room, and service line. Duties include quality food preparation through the use of standardized recipes; assisting the chef with recipe validation by verifying quantities of ingredients used, methods used, and resulting yield; and cleaning and maintaining appliances, production utensils, and work areas. Essential functions : Produces high quality food products by using approved cooking methods and by following standardized recipes. Accurately completes production sheets for all items produced in a timely manner (same day; preferably at end of meal). Works at action stations on the line, in the dining hall, and at events as assigned and prepares food quickly, with high quality, in a pleasant and entertaining manner. Ensures safety of self and others by following best practices defined by ServSafe, HACCP steps, and OSHA and college policies and procedures. Performs pre-meal/advanced preparation and JIT production using all the following methods of food production: broil, bake, stew, braise, roast, grill, sauté, and deep fry; also slices, dices, chops, mixes, marinates, and blends. Responsible for producing assigned foods; directing servers on proper portion size and service techniques/utensils/plating of assigned foods; and ensures assigned food is garnished and presented in an attractive manner. Cooperates with and supports all other employees and departments as needed. Performs any other duties as requested by management. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. Qualifications Required: High School Diploma or GED with 1-3 years of related experience. Preferred: Vocational or technical certificate/degree in Culinary Arts Current ServSafe certification or obtain certification within one year Physical Demands: This position requires the employee to stand for prolong periods of time. Employee must have the ability to lift 50 pounds as needed. Ability to use hands and fingers to manipulate equipment, knives and food products. Must be able to see-including color distinction, smell, and taste. Advertised Work Schedule Hours vary depending on business needs. This position will work both day and evening shifts starting as early as 5:30 a.m. and working as late as 10:00 p.m. for a total of 40 hours. Days off will vary depending on business needs. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dining-Service---Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Dining-Hall-Serving-Line---Kitchen-Janitorial-Casual_JR100536": {
      "title": "Dining Hall-Serving Line & Kitchen Janitorial Casual",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\nVariable time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department JM - Dining Services - Dining Hall Job Summary/Basic Function Dining Services supports campus food service operations. This role is ideal for individuals who enjoy working in a fast-paced environment and are committed to providing quality service to students, faculty, and staff. General Summary of Job Duties Odd Jobs • Taking out trash, recyclables or boxes as needed. • Check with the Chefs and Cooks as to which equipment needs to be cleaned up to and including large kettles, walls, wacks and other various equipment. • Work on any special tasks assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. • Cleaning tables, sinks, carts. • Sweeping, scrubbing and mopping of floors in the kitchen and serving areas • Cleaning of dock area. Pot Sink • Wash all pots and pans thoroughly. • Store all pots and pans upside down on appropriate shelves. • Clean all utensils brought to the pot sink and then store in appropriate areas. • Clean pot washing machine inside and out. • Clean all shelving and walls in pot sink area. • Taking out trash. • Sweep and mop floor in pot sink area. • Work on any special tasks as assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. Janitorial • Cleaning bathrooms. • Sweeping and mopping hallways and bathrooms. • Cleaning and vacuuming offices. • Sweeping and mopping floors in Dining Hall. • Sweeping and mopping Salad Department. • Taking out trash. • Cleaning refrigerator and freezer doors. • Cleaning hallway walls. • Assisting Odd Jobs or Pots as needed. • Work on any special tasks as assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. Serving • Assist in stocking, serving of food on our serving lines. • Cleaning of serving line areas. • Assisting on the grill serving line. • Making sandwiches, cutting desserts. • Any other special tasks as assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements: Must be 16 years old and some high school wanted. • Lifting up to 50 pounds • Food Handling • Prolonged Standing or Walking • Bending/Kneeling Personal Protective Equipment • Gloves • Towels for hot items • Protective eye wear when using chemical cleaners • Filter masks when using chemical cleaners EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dickinson-College/Retail-Operations-Attendant---Barista-9-month-PT_JR100516": {
      "title": "Retail Operations Attendant - Barista 9 month PT",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\nPart time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Retail Operations Job Summary/Basic Function Provides products and services to guests as appropriate to assigned retail location. Follows proper food handling techniques and recipes, delivers excellent customer service, maintains good sanitation and cleanliness practices, and provides customers with an enjoyable experience during all meal periods. Assists with training retail new staff as needed. May be assigned to various retail operation locations on campus. Primary duties Include: Attendants are responsible for positively greeting guests, providing excellent dining experiences and service to customers, preparing quality product utilizing recipes and all necessary equipment, and ensuring unit is well stocked and organized in a neat, clean manner. POS   register Food preparation (cold and hot) Non-alcoholic drink preparation General utility duties Assist in training staff Follows   HACCP   guidelines, Pennsylvania Department of Health regulations,   OSHA   regulations, safety policies, and ServSafe standards; ensures the cleanliness of prepartation areas, all seating, and serving areas; documents   HACCP   information such as food and equipment temperatures, times of food batches, packing data for food set-ups on the line, e.g. label information for pre-packaged deli salads. Assists guests with food allergies, special requests and customized preparation, and possesses a working knowledge of food ingredients. Follows policies and procedures to ensure that all facilities and equipment are left in the appropriate condition at the end of each shift. Follows proper cash handling policies and procedures. Promotes positive relationships within and outside of the department through effective communication. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. Other Duties May Include: Assist the Retail Operations Manager as needed. Detailed cleaning in units. Support special events and programs. Ensure a safe and inclusive environment is maintained in assigned location. Requirements: High School Diploma or   GED Experience in a food service operation preferred but not required. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Assistant-Director-for-Residence-Life_JR100501": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Residence Life",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Residence Life Job Summary/Basic Function Position Summary Consistent with the college’s mission of providing a useful education for engaged citizens, the Assistant Director will play an integral role in the residential experience, developing and implementing community initiatives and overseeing an environment that supports students in the complexities of living together. The incumbent works with the fellow staff to create a vision for community development within a liberal arts setting that intentionally supports an engaging academic and intellectual environment for students beyond the classroom walls. This live-in position creates and facilitates distinctive conditions and programs throughout the residential experience that intentionally foster community, promote curiosity, and seek engagement from its members so that they are able to thrive throughout their experience. The Assistant Director reports to the Associate Director of Campus Life for Residence Life & Housing. Essential Functions Provide leadership and oversight for a four-year residential community of approximately 500–700 students by fostering an inclusive, safe, and engaging living environment that supports student success and development. Maintain a visible presence through regular student engagement, which includes but not limited to, building walkthroughs, office hours, and community initiatives. Respond to student concerns by providing support, facilitating conflict resolution, coordinating room changes, making appropriate referrals, and collaborating with campus partners. Develop and implement programming aligned with the residential curriculum to promote student learning and community engagement. Maintain accurate records, monitor residential facilities with community advisors and resident advisors to address maintenance and safety concerns, and serve as a liaison among students, faculty, staff, and families to support effective residence life and housing operations. 30% Provide direct supervision, training, and evaluation of 1–2 community advisors (head resident advisors) and 18–22 resident advisors or 8 house and apartment managers through regular individual meetings, weekly staff meetings, and oversight of residential curriculum implementation. Manage administrative processes, purchasing, and budget reconciliation to support student staff programming and approved work-related purchases while ensuring compliance with departmental and institutional policies. 20% Serve as chair for one or more Residence Life and Housing committees, including Student Staff Selection, Student Staff Training, and Programmatic Curriculum, providing leadership in the planning, implementation, and assessment of departmental initiatives. Oversee one or more departmental focus areas, such as the First-Year Experience, Upper-Class Experience, or Housing Operations by developing strategies, coordinating initiatives, and collaborating with campus partners to advance departmental goals and enhance the residential student experience. 20% Develop and maintain collaborative partnerships with campus departments, community organizations, and external stakeholders to coordinate programs and services that enhance the residential experience. Collaborate with campus partners, including Public Safety, Facilities Management, and CASE, to support the effective operation of residential facilities, oversee residential key management, and ensure timely resolution of operational needs. Support and participate in Campus Life initiatives and maintain Residence Life and Housing website content to provide accurate and timely information to students and the campus community. 10% Provide 24/7 on-call crisis response and administrative support for the residential campus by participating in a four-person professional staff on-call rotation, serving as the college's Administrator on-call, and maintaining a required 30-minute response time while on-call. Assess and respond to student emergencies and critical incidents within the residential community, implementing appropriate crisis response protocols and collaborating with campus partners to ensure the safety, well-being, and support of students and the campus community. 10% Coordinate and oversee the opening and closing of residential facilities by collaborating with student staff to prepare buildings for occupancy, including the completion and management of Room Condition Reports. Supervise closing processes to ensure spaces are inspected, damages are accurately documented and assessed, and health and safety inspections are completed prior to residence hall break closings in compliance with institutional policies and standards. 10% Other Duties and Responsibilities This position is a 12-month live-in position. Assist with Campus Life special event planning and coordination. Participate in departmental, divisional, or college committees as appointed. Participate in the student conduct resolution process by facilitating the informal resolution process and administrative hearings for assigned cases as needed. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Counseling, Higher Education Administration, or related field, required. A valid driver’s license for the operation of a company-owned, rented or leased vehicle. Pennsylvania Act 153 Clearance consisting of the Pennsylvania Criminal History Record Information Check, Pennsylvania Child Abuse Certification, and Federal Criminal History Record Information Check pursuant to Pennsylvania law and Dickinson College policy. Experience in Residence Life and Housing, specifically within first-year programming, hall support, etc., is preferred, but not required. Experience working with eRezLife is preferred. Strong customer service skills to deal with situations tactfully and promptly. Flexible hours including nights and weekend commitments. Ability to routinely access student residence halls and other campus facilities, including walking throughout buildings and climbing and descending stairs in the course of performing job responsibilities, with or without a reasonable accommodation. Work Experience 1-3 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Standard office equipment. Physical and Environmental Demands Ability to routinely access student residence halls and other campus facilities, including walking throughout buildings and climbing and descending stairs in the course of performing job responsibilities, with or without a reasonable accommodation. Office environment. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Waidner-Spahr-Library/Student-Technology-Support---Engagement-Specialist_JR100504": {
      "title": "Student Technology Support & Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department User Services - Computing Specialists Job Summary/Basic Function The Student Technology Support & Engagement Specialist ensures effective IT support at Dickinson College by managing the student technical staff at the Help Desk, coordinating support for student-owned technology and maintaining the campus loaner laptop program. This position also creates technical documentation, maintains the User Services Knowledge Base and collaborates with User Services and Academic Technology liaisons. Lastly, this position serves as backup for the Help Desk when needed and communicates IT resources and services to campus. The Student Technology Support & Engagement Specialist ensures effective IT support at Dickinson College. They manage recruitment, training, scheduling, and supervision of student technical staff at the Help Desk and the ResNet Services Annex student computer support location. They coordinate support for student-owned technology and the campus loaner laptop program in conjunction with student-facing support. This position also creates technical documentation for campus-supported technologies and maintains the User Services Knowledge Base, ensuring the documentation is posted and updated as required. In the application of that technical knowledge, the position collaborates with User Services and Academic Technology liaisons on IT training for faculty, students, and staff as needed, including developing training materials, conducting workshops, and providing one-on-one support. The position serves as backup for the Help Desk when needed and communicates IT resources and services to the campus. Position requires strong communication, technical troubleshooting, and organizational skills. Position works independently and collaboratively within a dynamic support environment. Essential Functions This position is responsible for recruiting, hiring, training, scheduling, and supervising the User Services student technical team to ensure they are effectively integrated into departmental operations. The role oversees the daily functions of the Student Help Desk, ResNet Services Annex, and the Hardware Support Assistant positions, ensuring consistent and high-quality service delivery. Providing regular performance feedback, coaching, and mentorship to student employees is a key responsibility, supporting their development and success. Additionally, the position maintains and updates the student staff handbook, operational policies, and support workflows to reflect evolving procedures and uphold institutional standards. The position is responsible for maintaining and expanding User Services’ internal and public-facing Knowledge Base of technical documentation. This includes writing and editing clear, accurate how-to guides and collaborating with both professional and student staff to update existing materials. The role also involves evaluating current documentation systems and developing strategies to improve accessibility, usability, and overall effectiveness for a diverse user audience. This position plans and coordinates IT training opportunities for students, faculty, and staff, including workshops, orientation events, and drop-in support sessions. It involves partnering with departments, administrative offices, Computing Specialists, and Academic Technology to assess training needs and develop targeted instructional materials, with an emphasis on making relevant content available through the Knowledge Base. The role also represents User Services in campus initiatives and collaborates on technology onboarding activities related to the academic calendar. The role includes creating and distributing student-focused IT communications through email and other platforms, ensuring messages are clear, informative, and timely. It involves developing and implementing strategies to engage students through digital channels, with consideration for the effective use of social media where appropriate. Additionally, the position ensures the accurate and prompt dissemination of information related to service outages, system updates, and available technology resources. This position oversees the health, readiness, and imaging of the college’s loaner laptop fleets, ensuring that devices are properly maintained and fully functional. It includes coordinating with Help Desk staff to support efficient and consistent laptop checkout and check-in procedures. The role also involves maintaining system updates, performing diagnostics, and addressing technical issues as needed to keep the fleet in optimal working condition. The position serves as the designated backup to the full-time Help Desk Specialist, providing front-line user support during absences, high-demand periods, or other critical times. It also includes assisting with the mentoring of student staff by guiding them through escalated support issues and reinforcing Help Desk procedures to ensure consistent and effective service. Requirements Associate's Degree - Information Technology or a related field. 1-3 Years work experience Preferred Bachelor's Degree - Information Technology, Computer Science, Education, or a related discipline. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/John-M-Paz-Alumni--Family-Center/Temporary-Paz-Center_JR100607": {
      "title": "Temporary Paz Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nVariable time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Advancement - John M Paz Alumni and Family Center Position Details Temporary Office to support daily administrative operations. This short-term role is ideal for individuals with strong organizational skills and a proactive attitude. Responsibilities include answering phones, managing correspondence, scheduling appointments, maintaining records, and assisting with general office tasks. The ideal candidate will be proficient in Microsoft Office, possess excellent communication skills, and adapt quickly to new environments. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Biddle-House/Office-Coordinator-Registrar-s-Office_JR100603": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator Registrar's Office",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Registrar's Office Position Details The Registrar Office Coordinator is most often the first contact the students, parents, faculty, and staff have with the Registrar’s Office. The first impression that is given is an important part of how the office is perceived, thus the information services coordinator must be personable, professional and knowledgeable of the functions of the office. Greeting, meeting, answering questions, directing people/questions appropriately, and supervising student workers are the main responsibilities of the position. The Registrar Office Coordinator is often the first contact the students, parents, faculty, and staff have with the Registrar’s Office. The position provides front-line customer service and administrative support by monitoring, answering, and directing phone calls, emails, and walk in inquiries and assisting with building related functions. The Coordinator processes key academic and administrative forms, ensuring proper approvals and resolving documentation issues. Additional responsibilities include preparing and distributing Dean’s List letters, supporting student employee hiring and supervision, updating office procedure manuals and emergency plans, and coordinating placement and AP credit posting for students. Essential Functions: Customer Service/Administrative Support to the Associate Registrar - Monitor, answer, and direct to the appropriate personphone calls and walk-ins to the Registrar’s Office. Schedule individual appointments for the Associate Registrar. Providedirectional support to students in-person and remotely, when needed. Assist with the coordination of Registrar’s Office/BiddleHouse Functions. Forms Processing - Communicate with faculty and students regarding needed approvals and missing documentation, as well as respond to inquiries about the online Enrollment in Another Institution Form. Process FERPA Recommendation Letter requests, Pass/Fail forms, Permanent Home address changes, and notices received about deceased alumni. requests, Pass/Fail forms, Permanent Home address changes, and notices received about deceased alumni. E-mails/Correspondence - Monitor, answer, and direct e-mails to the appropriate person from the Registrar’s e-mail account.Maintain a collection of standard email responses for use by the Registrar’s staff for a variety of inquiries. Prepare anddistribute Dean’s List letters each semester and on adhoc basis. Open, sort and distribute mail. Scan documents and fileinto Content 7. Student Employment - Hire/supervise student employees, including interviewing, scheduling, training, time approval for pay & coordinating duties Office Procedures - Maintain Office Procedures Manual. Update Check-Off lists used throughout the year. Building Coordinator for Department Emergency Plan - Update and maintain Department Emergency Plan. Coordinate with other departments in building to keep information accurate. Keep in contact with the appropriate person in DPS for updates with Emergency Plan. Placement & Credit – Coordinate and post AP credit, as well as language, math, chemistry and music placement information for students not automatically loaded into the system. Other Duties and Responsibilities • Process transcript requests. • Assist with section creation. • Execute scripts related to job functions. • Other duties as determined or assigned. Requirements • Required: High school diploma or equivalent, required. • Preferred: Associate's degree, preferred 1-3 Years Work Experience EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Cook_JR100601": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Kitchen Position Details This is a hands-on food production position. The cook must have the ability to work in all production stations in the kitchen, dining room, and service line. Duties include quality food preparation through the use of standardized recipes; assisting the chef with recipe validation by verifying quantities of ingredients used, methods used, and resulting yield; and cleaning and maintaining appliances, production utensils, and work areas. Essential functions : Produces high quality food products by using approved cooking methods and by following standardized recipes. Accurately completes production sheets for all items produced in a timely manner (same day; preferably at end of meal). Works at action stations on the line, in the dining hall, and at events as assigned and prepares food quickly, with high quality, in a pleasant and entertaining manner. Ensures safety of self and others by following best practices defined by ServSafe, HACCP steps, and OSHA and college policies and procedures. Performs pre-meal/advanced preparation and JIT production using all the following methods of food production: broil, bake, stew, braise, roast, grill, sauté, and deep fry; also slices, dices, chops, mixes, marinates, and blends. Responsible for producing assigned foods; directing servers on proper portion size and service techniques/utensils/plating of assigned foods; and ensures assigned food is garnished and presented in an attractive manner. Cooperates with and supports all other employees and departments as needed. Performs any other duties as requested by management. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. Qualifications Required: High School Diploma or GED with 1-3 years of related experience. Preferred: Vocational or technical certificate/degree in Culinary Arts Current ServSafe certification or obtain certification within one year Physical Demands: This position requires the employee to stand for prolong periods of time. Employee must have the ability to lift 50 pounds as needed. Ability to use hands and fingers to manipulate equipment, knives and food products. Must be able to see-including color distinction, smell, and taste. Advertised Work Schedule Hours vary depending on business needs. This position will work both day and evening shifts starting as early as 5:30 a.m. and working as late as 10:00 p.m. for a total of 40 hours. Days off will vary depending on business needs. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Facilities-Management/Groundskeeper-I_JR100600": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Facilities Management - Grounds and Landscaping Position Details A Groundskeeper I functions as a working member of the College’s grounds crew or as a project leader, in performing various duties to maintain and assure and attractive appearance of the campus though the execution of daily and planned maintenance activities. Crew members are expected to maintain their individual campus zone with minimal supervision and direction. Crew members should be able to plan, prioritize and execute their activities such that the required work gets done with minimal intervention from their supervisor(s). Essential Functions Maintains individual campus zone including mowing, fertilizing policing, irrigating, seeding,aerating, pruning, planting, leaf collection, etc. Ensures work is done in a safe and productive manner. Ensures that all trash and recycling receptacles are monitored and emptied as needed. Monitors pedestrian traffic areas for debris, appearance and safety issues. Blows off walks and performs other maintenance as needed. Also monitors storm drains and keeps clear. Makes pesticide applications and maintains pesticide application log. Attends safety and pesticide update trainings as required. Operates all grounds equipment in a safe and professional manner. Perform maintenance and minor repairs on grounds equipment. Assists grounds lead and Director of Grounds with supervising the work of student labor. Trains the groundskeeper II and student labor in maintenance and landscaping skills. Works with other grounds crew members to remove snow from campus sidewalks, parking lots, driveways, and steps. All grounds crew members are considered “essential employees.” As such they are required to report to work even when the college is closed or is operating under a delayed start. Grounds crew members can be called in at any time of day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. It is expected that the employee has reliable transportation adequate to transport them to work even under adverse weather conditions. Requirements Education: Required: Diploma GED Preferred: Bachelors Degree in Horticulture, landscaping contracting Must have a PA Commercial Pesticide Applicator License Category 23 Parks/Schools Pest Control, or obtain within six months of hire. Must have a PA Class B CDL. Ability to obtain a Forklift Operators certification. This position requires a valid driver's license for the operation of a company owned, rented or leased vehicle. 1-3 Years Work Experience EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    }
  },
